# 11. ML Inference Architecture

## 11.1 Proposed Architecture

The existing MERN application remains the primary business application.

The ML inference component should be isolated from the Express backend.

Proposed flow:

```text
React Frontend
      |
      v
Express Backend
      |
      | Authentication
      | Ownership Validation
      | Image Validation
      | Analysis Request
      |
      v
Python FastAPI Inference API
      |
      v
Image Preprocessing
      |
      v
Image Quality Assessment
      |
      v
Condition Classification Model
      |
      v
Defect Classification Model
      |
      v
Confidence and Uncertainty Evaluation
      |
      v
Structured Prediction Response
      |
      v
Express Backend
      |
      v
MongoDB Atlas
      |
      v
React Analysis Report
```

The Python service must not independently manage customer accounts, deck ownership, or application permissions.

Those responsibilities remain with Express.

## 11.2 Service Responsibilities

### Express Backend

Responsible for:

- Authentication.
- Authorization.
- Deck ownership verification.
- Image ownership verification.
- Analysis request creation.
- Calling the ML service.
- Validating inference responses.
- Saving analysis records.
- Returning results to the frontend.
- Managing analysis history.

### Python FastAPI Service

Responsible for:

- Loading the approved model.
- Receiving permitted image input.
- Preprocessing images.
- Assessing image quality.
- Running condition inference.
- Running defect inference.
- Evaluating confidence.
- Returning structured results.
- Reporting model version and inference status.

### MongoDB

Responsible for:

- Analysis records.
- Prediction snapshots.
- Model version references.
- Analysis status.
- Image references.
- Error and review metadata.

Do not store large image binaries directly inside analysis documents.

Use the existing Phase 4 media-storage mechanism and store image references.

