# 12. ML API Specification

## 12.1 Health Endpoint

`GET /health`

Purpose:

Check whether the ML inference service is available.

Example:

```json
{
  "status": "healthy",
  "service": "deck-condition-analysis",
  "modelLoaded": true,
  "modelVersion": "1.0.0"
}
```

## 12.2 Prediction Endpoint

`POST /api/v1/analyze`

Purpose:

Analyze one deck photograph.

The service should receive an authorized image reference or image data through a controlled backend-to-ML integration.

Do not expose unrestricted private image-storage URLs.

Example request:

```json
{
  "analysisId": "analysis-001",
  "imageReference": "internal-image-reference",
  "deckSurface": "wood"
}
```

The image reference is illustrative. The final transport mechanism must be selected after reviewing Phase 4 storage.

## 12.3 Example Successful Response

```json
{
  "analysisId": "analysis-001",
  "status": "COMPLETED",
  "imageQuality": {
    "label": "GOOD",
    "confidence": 0.96
  },
  "condition": {
    "level": 3,
    "label": "MODERATE_DETERIORATION",
    "confidence": 0.87
  },
  "defects": [
    {
      "label": "PEELING_COATING",
