# 18. Testing Strategy

Phase 7 must include ML tests, backend integration tests, frontend validation, and full regression testing.

## 18.1 Dataset Tests

Verify:

- Invalid images are rejected.
- Duplicate images are identified.
- Missing labels are detected.
- Unsupported labels are rejected.
- Dataset splits do not leak images from the same deck.
- Class distributions are reported.
- Annotation status is validated.

## 18.2 ML Model Tests

Evaluate:

- Five-level classification.
- Multi-label defect classification.
- Image-quality assessment.
- Confidence scoring.
- Uncertain predictions.
- Poor-quality photographs.
- Unseen deck examples.

### Required Evaluation Metrics

For severity classification:

- Accuracy.
- Precision.
- Recall.
- F1-score.
- Confusion matrix.
- Per-class performance.

For defect classification:

- Precision per defect.
- Recall per defect.
- F1-score per defect.
- Multi-label evaluation metrics.

For confidence:

- Calibration evaluation.
- Coverage versus error when abstaining.
- Manual-review rate.

Do not report accuracy alone.

A model can achieve high overall accuracy while performing poorly on Level 5.

The developer must report the performance of every condition level separately.

## 18.3 Backend Tests

Test:

- Authentication.
- Customer ownership.
- Contractor authorization.
- Admin permissions.
- Analysis creation.
- Image-reference validation.
- ML API communication.
- Invalid ML response handling.
- Analysis persistence.
- Analysis history.
- Retry behavior.
